.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt KST 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm kst
.Nd one screen of a kldload machine's health
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Nm
.Fl h | -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
prints, on one screen:
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
the host name, the kldload edition and the build it was installed from;
.It
the address this machine uses to reach the internet;
.It
.Li rpool Ns 's
health and its error summary;
.It
the running boot environment's space used and available, and its
compression;
.It
the number of snapshots on the machine, and when the newest was taken;
.It
how many boot environments there are;
.It
memory in use, processors, uptime;
.It
whether
.Pa kldload-webui ,
.Pa sshd ,
.Pa zfs-zed ,
.Pa sanoid.timer
and
.Pa NetworkManager
are active:
.Ql ●
active,
.Ql ○
not,
.Ql ✗
failed.
.El
.Pp
On a terminal the pool's dot is green, yellow when degraded and red
otherwise; piped, the output is plain text.
.Pp
It reports; it does not judge, and exits 0 whatever it finds.
.Xr kldload-doctor 8
judges.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print the usage and exit 0.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /etc/kldload/edition
The edition.
.It Pa /etc/kldload-build-sha
The build.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width 1n -compact
.It 0
Printed.
.It 2
An argument was given.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Printed on a kldload desktop on 2026-09-30.
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ kst

  kldload onyx  (free edition, build 510236f5)
  IP         10.100.10.121

  Pool       ● rpool ONLINE  (No known data errors)
  Root       343G used / 166G available  (compression: 1.04x)
  Snapshots  2122 total  (newest: Wed Sep 30  0:00 2026)
  Boot envs  1 available
  Memory     19Gi / 31Gi  |  CPUs  24  |  Uptime  1 day, 18 hours, 7 minutes

  Services   ● kldload-webui  ● sshd  ● zfs-zed  ● sanoid.timer  ● NetworkManager

# (exited 0)
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr kdf 8 ,
.Xr kldload-doctor 8 ,
.Xr kldload-rollback 8 ,
.Xr ksnap 8
.Sh HISTORY
It once crashed without printing anything on a pool with 345 snapshots:
the snapshot list outgrew a pipe that a reader closed early.
.Pp
On 2026-09-30, writing this page:
.Fl -help
printed the dashboard; with no boot environments the count read
.Ql 0
twice; the address was read from a fixed field that moves with the
route; and on a host without
.Li rpool
it stopped silently part-way.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An kldload Aq Mt anthony@kldload.com
.Sh CAVEATS
The services listed are a fixed five.
A machine installed without the web console shows it as not active,
which is correct and not a fault.
